blurb: In a tense budget workshop, the BOARD OF EDUCATION debated the FY26 Superintendent’s
  Budget, focusing on restoring cut student-facing positions like SEL teachers by
  potentially freezing administrative salaries. Faced with deep divisions and a last-minute
  offer from principals to find savings, the board failed to pass a budget and will
  continue deliberations at a future meeting.
